   "tips": [
    "<b>Same Middle C position as before.</b> Left hand fingers 5 4 3 2 1 on F G A B C, right hand fingers 1 2 3 4 5 on C D E F G. Your hands never move.",
    "<b>Wait before you start.</b> Bar 1 begins with 2 beats of silence. Count \"1, 2\" quietly, then play \"A\" on beat 3.",
    "<b>Only one hand plays at a time.</b> The hands take turns, like two sailors passing a rope.",
    "<b>Both thumbs share Middle C.</b> In bar 3, the left thumb plays \"sea\", then the right thumb plays \"To\" on the same key. Lift the left thumb as the right one comes down. Same in bars 5 and 7.",
    "<b>The left hand pattern comes twice:</b> C, then F F A A (fingers 1, 5 5 3 3). Learn it once, use it twice.",
    "<b>The right hand jumps over a key:</b> F F D D (fingers 4 4 2 2). Skip E on the way down.",
    "<b>The ending climbs like a wave:</b> C C D D E E F (fingers 1 1 2 2 3 3 4). Hold the last F for 2 beats.",
    "<b>\"Quite fast\" comes last.</b> Learn it slowly first, then move the speed up a little each day."
