   "tips": [
    "<b>Middle C position.</b> Both thumbs share Middle C. Left hand fingers 5 4 3 2 1 sit on F G A B C. Right hand fingers 1 2 3 4 5 sit on C D E F G. Every note of this piece is under a finger, so your hands never move.",
    "<b>Line 1 is the musical alphabet.</b> It walks up A B C D E F G, then walks back down. There are only 7 letters: after G, the alphabet starts again at A.",
    "<b>Pass the tune between hands.</b> Left hand plays A and B, then the right thumb takes over on C. Make the handover so smooth it sounds like one hand.",
    "<b>White notes with a stem last 2 beats.</b> Hold G at the end of bars 2 and 4, and the last C. Count \"1 2 3 4\" in every bar.",
    "<b>Line 2 is the same idea in solfa.</b> So fa mi re do ti la so. On this page, do is always C.",
    "<b>In bar 6 the left thumb plays do (C).</b> The right hand has just finished on D, so let the left hand catch the tune.",
    "<b>Bar 7 starts low, on F.</b> That is left-hand finger 5 (the F your teacher wrote). Climb F G A B, then the right thumb finishes on C.",
    "<b>\"Smoothly\" means legato.</b> Let each key come up just as the next one goes down. No gaps, no bumps."
