   "tips": [
    "<b>Tango is a dance for two people</b> from Argentina and Uruguay. It sounds sharp and jumpy, like dancers stepping and stopping.",
    "<b>Play 2 keys at the same time.</b> Most notes here are pairs of keys. Press both together, as if they were one key. In the app, tap both keys (one after the other is fine) to move on.",
    "<b>Every note is short and strong.</b> The dot means staccato: bounce off the key quickly. The &gt; means accent: play it a bit louder.",
    "<b>The rests are part of the dance.</b> Your teacher boxed them in pencil. Keep counting \"1 2 3 4\" out loud, and stay silent on the rests. Silence on beat 3 is what makes it sound like a tango.",
    "<b>Bars 1 and 2:</b> left hand plays A and C together (fingers 3 and 1). The right hand answers with one E (finger 3) on beat 3.",
    "<b>Bar 3: the left hand moves down.</b> The pink circle in the book means a new hand position. Thumb on A, finger 3 on F. Use the rest at the end of bar 2 to move.",
    "<b>Bar 7: both hands play together.</b> Right hand D and E (fingers 2 and 3), left hand B (finger 2). Your left thumb is back on Middle C.",
    "<b>The last note is three keys:</b> right hand C and E, left hand A. Then three beats of silence. Freeze like a dancer at the end!"
   ]
  }
 ]
